**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** Opening a folder the user picked, in Domain: initialise it when it holds no kit, open it otherwise (001 §F 'New kit…: … An empty folder is initialised; a folder that already has files keeps them, and .kit-json plus the app's subfolders are added'; 001 §E 'an open read-only choice'; the S4.3 brief: Main and Inverse open a kit through a `KitFolderPicker` seam, a Domain record, followed by S4.1's initialise-or-open; .spec-md §3.10). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Kit.fs`, beside `KitFolder.tryKitPathOf` (step 132): `type KitFolder with member this.namedKitFile (id : KitId) (author : KitAuthor) (now : ClockTime) : Result<KitFile, KitError>` is `KitFile.create id <name> author now` (step 122), the name being `KitName.tryCreate` of the folder's leaf: its text with every `\` turned into `/` and trailing `/` removed, after the last `/`. A blank leaf (a drive root such as `C:/`) answers `InvalidKitNameErr`. It touches no disk. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/KitFolders.fs`, after `KitContext` (step 131): (a) `[<ReferenceEquality>] KitFolderPicker = { pickKitFolder : unit -> Async<KitFolder option> }`, how the app asks the user for a kit folder; `None` when the user cancels. The brief writes the field `unit -> KitFolder option`; it answers `Async` because Avalonia's folder dialog (`IStorageProvider.OpenFolderPickerAsync`) completes asynchronously on the UI thread, and blocking the dispatcher on it deadlocks. The App passes the Avalonia dialog (steps 150, 154); headless tests pass a folder under the test output (step 154); S5.2's start screen calls the same seam. (b) `type KitContext with static member openOrInitialise (proxy : KitProxy) (clock : ClockProvider) (newKitFile : ClockTime -> Result<KitFile, KitError>) : Result<KitContext, KitError>` is `KitContext.openKit proxy ReadWriteKitAccess clock` (step 131); on `NotAKitFolderErr` only it calls `newKitFile (clock.now ())`, then `proxy.initialiseKit` of that kit file (step 125), then `openKit` read-write again. Every other error passes through and nothing is written, `KitLockedErr` included: the caller may then open the kit with `ReadOnlyKitAccess` (001 §E). A folder that is a kit keeps its kit file, and `newKitFile` is not called. (c) `static member createInMemory (kitFile : KitFile) (clock : ClockProvider) : KitContext`: a new `InMemoryKitFolder` (step 125) holding exactly what `initialiseKit kitFile` leaves (the kit file, `data` and `library`), and a context over the folder's first proxy holding that kit file, `ReadWriteKitAccess` and the clock. It takes no lock and records no stamp, because no other proxy can reach the folder, so it cannot fail and answers the context. It is the kit of a scene that opened no folder (step 150). No other member, option or verb is added, and `KitProxy` gains no field. Tests. `KitTests` (step 122) gains `a new kit is named for its folder`: `namedKitFile` over `KitFolder (FolderName "C:/kits/Optics QZ")`, over `C:\kits\Optics QZ\` and over `C:/kits/Optics QZ/` answers a kit file named `Optics QZ` with the given id, author and instant (`created` equal to `modified`); over `C:/` it answers `InvalidKitNameErr`. New `KitProxyContract` facts (step 125), so `KitProxyTests` and `KitProxyFolderTests` both run them, each passing `newKitFile clock` (step 125) wrapped in `Ok` as the new kit file: `opening a folder that holds no kit initialises it and opens it read-write`: over a fresh folder, `openOrInitialise` of proxy A answers a context holding that kit file and `ReadWriteKitAccess`, and `paths` is exactly `.kit-json`, `.oc`, `.oc/lock`, `data` and `library`. `opening a folder that is a kit keeps its kit file`: over a folder initialised with the kit file whose notes are `KitNotes "first"`, `openOrInitialise` of A whose new kit file has another id answers the first kit file, and B's `readKitFile` answers it unchanged. `a kit open elsewhere is not opened or initialised again`: with A opened through `openOrInitialise`, B's `openOrInitialise` answers `KitLockedErr` of A's holder, a test-local counter of its new-kit calls stays 0, and `paths` is unchanged; `KitContext.openKit` of B with `ReadOnlyKitAccess` then answers a context. `KitProxyTests` (in memory only) gains `an in-memory kit context holds its kit file and writes through its own folder`: `KitContext.createInMemory` of `newKitFile clock` answers a context holding that kit file and `ReadWriteKitAccess`; its `proxy.readKitFile` answers that kit file, and `proxy.writeKindFile ExperimentKitFile (FileStem "E1")` of a text, then `readKindFile`, answers that text.

**Acceptance.** After the open seam lands, `KitContext.openOrInitialise` MUST initialise a folder that holds no kit and open a kit read-write keeping its kit file, passing `KitLockedErr` through with nothing written, and `KitFolder.namedKitFile` MUST name a new kit for its folder; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a new kit is named for its folder`, `opening a folder that holds no kit initialises it and opens it read-write`, `opening a folder that is a kit keeps its kit file`, `a kit open elsewhere is not opened or initialised again` under `KitProxyTests` and `KitProxyFolderTests`, and `an in-memory kit context holds its kit file and writes through its own folder`, the count rising by 8; and build, elevation and the eleven s17 invariants MUST pass.
